    "body": "Effy is operated by [LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME] (ABN [ABN]) (\"Effy\", \"we\", \"us\", \"our\"). This\nPrivacy Policy explains what personal information we collect when you use the Effy website and mobile\napps, why we collect it, who we share it with, how long we keep it, and the choices and rights you\nhave. We handle personal information in accordance with the *Privacy Act 1988* (Cth) and the Australian\nPrivacy Principles (APPs).\n\nThis is a draft prepared for legal review. By using Effy you acknowledge this Privacy Policy. It should\nbe read together with our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) and our\n[Cookie & Tracking Notice](/legal/cookies-tracking).\n\n## Who we are\n\nThe entity responsible for your personal information is [LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME], ABN [ABN], of\n[REGISTERED_ADDRESS]. If you have any question about this policy or your personal information, contact\nus at hello@effyshopping.com.\n\n## What personal information we collect\n\nWe collect only the information we need to run the service. Depending on how you use Effy, this may\ninclude:\n\n- **Account identity** — your name and email address, and, if you choose \"Sign in with Google\", the\n  verified email and basic profile the provider returns.\n- **Contact and delivery details** — the delivery addresses and contact details you add.\n- **Order and purchase history** — the items you order, when, and to where.\n- **Payment records** — a record that a payment was made and its amount. Card details are entered\n  directly into our payment processor and are **never stored by Effy**.\n- **Saved items and cart** — the products you save or add to your basket, including as a guest.\n- **Device and notification data** — a push-notification token and basic device information, so we can\n  send order updates you have asked for.\n- **Product-interaction and usage data** — how you use the app and website, to keep it working and\n  improve it.\n- **Crash and diagnostic data** — technical reports when the app fails, so we can fix it.\n- **Support communications** — the messages you send us and our replies.\n\nWe do **not** collect precise location, and we do **not** track you across other companies' apps or\nwebsites for advertising.\n\n## How we collect it\n\nWe collect most of this information directly from you — when you create an account, place an order, save\nan item, or contact us. Some information (usage, crash and device data) is collected automatically as\nyou use the service, as described in our [Cookie & Tracking Notice](/legal/cookies-tracking). Where the\nlaw requires, we tell you at or before the time we collect (APP 5).\n\n## Why we use it\n\nWe use personal information to:\n\n- create and manage your account and verify it is you;\n- take, fulfil and deliver your orders, and process payments and refunds;\n- keep the service secure and prevent fraud;\n- send you service messages and, where you have consented, marketing;\n- provide customer support; and\n- understand and improve how Effy works.\n\n## Marketing\n\nWe only send marketing email where you have consented, and every marketing message includes an\nunsubscribe link. You can opt out at any time without affecting the service messages you need (such as\norder confirmations). This is consistent with APP 7 and the *Spam Act 2003* (Cth).\n\n## Who we share it with\n\nWe do not sell your personal information. We share it only with service providers who help us run Effy,\nand only for the purposes above. These include:\n\n- **Amazon Web Services** — identity, our application database, media storage and transactional email.\n- **Stripe** — payment processing.\n- **PostHog** — product analytics and error tracking.\n- **Google (Firebase)** and **Apple** — crash reporting and push-notification delivery.\n- **Google** — optional \"Sign in with Google\".\n\nWe may also disclose information where required or authorised by law, or to protect the safety of our\ncustomers, our staff, or the public.\n\n## Overseas disclosure\n\nSome of our service providers process information outside Australia, including in the United States.\nWhere we disclose personal information overseas (APP 8), we take reasonable steps to ensure it is\nhandled consistently with the APPs.\n\n## How long we keep it\n\nWe keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purposes above, or as the law requires.\n\nWhen you delete your account, we remove your account, your saved items, your saved addresses and your\npersonal details. We keep the following, because the law or the safety of others requires it:\n\n- completed orders (tax and accounting obligations);\n- payment records (tax, accounting and fraud obligations); and\n- fraud and security signals that protect other customers.\n\n## Deleting your account and your data\n\nYou can delete your account at any time from within the Effy app or website, at **Account → Privacy &\ndata → Delete account**, or from [effyshopping.com/delete-account](https://effyshopping.com/delete-account) — you\ndo not need the app installed. When you confirm, your account is closed straight away, your sessions\nend, and you can no longer sign in. The records listed under \"How long we keep it\" are retained as\ndescribed there.\n\n## Keeping it secure\n\nWe take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, loss, and unauthorised access\n(APP 11), including encryption in transit, access controls, and isolated authentication. No method is\nperfectly secure, but we work to protect your information and to respond to incidents, including\nnotifying you and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) where the Notifiable Data\nBreaches scheme requires.\n\n## Accessing and correcting your information\n\nYou can view and update much of your information in the app under **Account**. You may also ask us for a\ncopy of the personal information we hold about you, or to correct it, by emailing\nhello@effyshopping.com (APP 12 and APP 13). We may need to verify your identity first.\n\n## Children\n\nEffy is intended for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect personal information from\nchildren. If you believe a child has provided us personal information, contact hello@effyshopping.com.\n\n## Complaints\n\nIf you have a concern about how we handle your personal information, contact us first at\nhello@effyshopping.com and we will try to resolve it. You may also complain to the Office of the\nAustralian Information Commissioner at oaic.gov.au.\n\n## Changes to this policy\n\nWe may update this policy from time to time. The current version and its effective date are always\nshown at the top, and previous versions are available from the version history.\n\n## Contact us\n\n[LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME]\nABN [ABN]\n[REGISTERED_ADDRESS]\nEmail: hello@effyshopping.com",
